{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension","id":1034596,"title":"Preview: Sariras - Relics of Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T07:41:46-08:00","id":1034596,"title":"Preview: Sariras - Relics of Ascension","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening\" target=\"_blank\">Check it out here</a>.<br /> <br /> One quick question Malcolm, which of the Pala Dynasties is The King Who Is A Throne supposed to refer to? There are three of them, and all of them are fairly geographically and temporally similar.<br /> <br /> <u><b>EDIT</b></u>: Reading comprehension. You said Pala Empire, not Dynasty, so that answers that question. Adding the Resonance bit to the Sariras is also interesting, it opens up the possibility to crossovers with other gamelines that use ephemeral entities. It would also be interesting to see how Mummies interact with the Sariras, since Ascension and Descent opposites in more ways than just linguistically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:56:06-08:00","id":1034674,"title":"","content":"Very nice.<br /> <br /> A question: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supernal Tool: A Sarira provides the benefits of dedicated magical tool for any mage who belongs to the same Path as the Ascended, but doesn\u2019t require attuning or impose a closer sympathetic connection. Consequently, as the manifestation of another willworker\u2019s Ascension, it cannot be dedicated for any additional benefit. </div> </div> </div>What if the Sarira is from an Ascended Archmage who no longer has a normal Path? Will the Sarira then act as a dedicated magical tool for mages of any Path?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:03:39-08:00","id":1034680,"title":"","content":"I assume it would be based off whatever Path his highest Arcana comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:04:01-08:00","id":1034681,"title":"","content":"Huh. That's a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm left most intrigued by the mention of Resonance Traits. Resonance is my Thing; it and sympathy are two of my favourite things from Mage. Maybe not mechanically, but definitely conceptually.<br /> <br /> The King itself got a laugh from me at the &quot;Throw a pillow on him&quot; line. I admit, Sariras don't hold my love so much because I can't really get my mind around disassembling a corpse for parts, but this is as close as one has probably gotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:10:18-08:00","id":1034686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034681#post1034681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. That's a thing.<br /> <br /> I can't really get my mind around disassembling a corpse for parts</div> </div> </div> </div>I then assume you don't normally play a Moros? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:12:40-08:00","id":1034688,"title":"","content":"It's not really even a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:21:17-08:00","id":1034691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034681#post1034681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really get my mind around disassembling a corpse for parts</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you could never have been a devout premodern Catholic or Orthodox, They did it all the time with saints' bodies and personal possessions.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, there are very good pragmatic reasons to keep Sariras intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:22:06-08:00","id":1034692,"title":"","content":"Chopping body of a saint into pieces? It's funny how Christian it is. <br /> My first thought was that rules are a little overcomplicated but as an inspiration it's really great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:25:59-08:00","id":1034697,"title":"","content":"There's that.<br /> <br /> Plus it's likely in one piece because one mage found it, and he's still torn about what exactly to do with it. Imagine two mages, or an entire cabal, each with their own ideas about how to use its power. You'd practically have to split it up. Especially if they were a lower power one, who wouldn't be able to defend themselves if someone came after the singular artifact.<br /> <br /> It's a neat write-up. And the spells are pretty powerful. I, too, am curious about the Resonance thing. I'm guessing it'll tie into the expanded yantras section but wonder if it would be something applicable in werewolf, since that seems to be written by the Werewolf dev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:38:10-08:00","id":1034705,"title":"","content":"I fucking love this sample sarira writeup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But he found the King performing a humble service, as a seat for the odd yogi to relax in between periods of exercise. The King Who Is a Throne has fused with his stool. He sat up straight, hands on his knees but elbows out, and he was a big man, too. Throw a cushion on there, and he\u2019d be quite comfortable to sit on. Yang\u2019s research uncovered a history of petty occultists and feudal lords who used the King this way for special occasions. Many of them burned to death. So did their palaces. So did forests and farms surrounding the palaces. </div> </div> </div>This is gold. Perfected Gold, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:45:03-08:00","id":1034751,"title":"","content":"Am I missing something in the sample Sarira, or is it only a 7 dot Artifact? The cost of an Artifact is the highest Arcana used in its highest spell, plus half the rating rounded up for each additional spell. That's 4 + 2 (half the Forces spell) + 1 (half the Mind spell) for 7. Does each spell include the Sympathetic Attainment for an additional 3 dots and I missed it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:47:38-08:00","id":1034754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034751#post1034751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something in the sample Sarira, or is it only a 7 dot Artifact? The cost of an Artifact is the highest Arcana used in its highest spell, plus half the rating rounded up for each additional spell. That's 4 + 2 (half the Forces spell) + 1 (half the Mind spell) for 7. Does each spell include the Sympathetic Attainment for an additional 3 dots and I missed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like they went with straight dot values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:50:33-08:00","id":1034757,"title":"","content":"The sarira systems override existing rules. And a sarira, intact, is always 10 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:44:51-08:00","id":1034786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034686#post1034686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I then assume you don't normally play a Moros? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thyrsus pride, baby!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034691#post1034691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you could never have been a devout premodern Catholic or Orthodox, They did it all the time with saints' bodies and personal possessions.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, there are very good pragmatic reasons to keep Sariras intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar with the cultural precedent - I've actually gotten to see a relic before; it was a piece of mummified forearm wrapped in a cast bronze arm, and if you grew up in Eastern Canada, you might know which one it was - but I just can't <i>get</i> it, myself.<br /> <br /> Maybe it just comes from my own history with doing dissections, but I cannot imagine slicing open a human being, pulling out what's inside, and treating it as magical. The symbolism just isn't there for me. Not unless the symbolism is meat or death, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Also, corpses just feel so... Awkward. Bodies aren't neat and tidy things; once the few kilograms of fat and salt that controls your flappy skinsuit decides to give up the ghost, you just kinda flop about. There's a reason morticians have to spend <i>so much</i> <i>time</i> preparing corpses for viewings; often having to pin down eyelids and bind arms and legs and stage the body in a box because if you just put a human cadaver anywhere, it flops like a rag doll.<br /> <br /> So when someone talks about using what is, for all intents and purposes, a corpse as a magical tool, all I can think is this really awkward hoisting of a body by what amounts to a highschool skeleton stand and using wires to pose the arms and legs in what is could qualify as the world's most heinous Thunderbirds homage but definitely not a magical ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:51:30-08:00","id":1034791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034757#post1034757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sarira systems override existing rules. And a sarira, intact, is always 10 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it says they have the power of 10 dot artifacts. This one doesn't.<br /> <br /> It has the powers of a 7 dot artifact. Nothing in the writeup indicates that the 'value' of the artifact is calculated any differently from normal artifacts, so the caveat that it might override normal rules doesn't really come into play.<br /> <br /> It honestly just looks like an oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:56:19-08:00","id":1034800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034791#post1034791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it says they have the power of 10 dot artifacts. This one doesn't.<br /> <br /> It has the powers of a 7 dot artifact. Nothing in the writeup indicates that the 'value' of the artifact is calculated any differently from normal artifacts, so the caveat that it might override normal rules doesn't really come into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most artifacts can't be divided up into smaller bits without losing their powers or store 200 Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:59:21-08:00","id":1034802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034800#post1034800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most artifacts can't be divided up into smaller bits without losing their powers or store 200 Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the value of those effects = 3 artifact dots, or if it's just calculated differently, that should still be made explicit, not implied through a sample.<br /> It's an oversight either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:04:12-08:00","id":1034805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034802#post1034802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the value of those effects = 3 artifact dots, or if it's just calculated differently, that should still be made explicit, not implied through a sample.<br /> It's an oversight either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It explicitly says that it has the power of a 10 dot artifact <i>plus</i> the following: Supernally Incorruptible, Divisible, Dynamic Artifact, Body of Mana, Resonance, and Supernal Tool.<br /> <br /> As for having 200 Mana, a normal Artifact contains mana equal to twice the dot rating. The write up says each Sarira dot possesses 10 points of mana. I believe 200 mana may also be an error and it should be 100. Either that or 20 points of mana per Sarira dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:05:49-08:00","id":1034807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034786#post1034786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thyrsus pride, baby!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm familiar with the cultural precedent - I've actually gotten to see a relic before; it was a piece of mummified forearm wrapped in a cast bronze arm, and if you grew up in Eastern Canada, you might know which one it was - but I just can't <i>get</i> it, myself.<br /> <br /> Maybe it just comes from my own history with doing dissections, but I cannot imagine slicing open a human being, pulling out what's inside, and treating it as magical. The symbolism just isn't there for me. Not unless the symbolism is meat or death, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Also, corpses just feel so... Awkward. Bodies aren't neat and tidy things; once the few kilograms of fat and salt that controls your flappy skinsuit decides to give up the ghost, you just kinda flop about. There's a reason morticians have to spend <i>so much</i> <i>time</i> preparing corpses for viewings; often having to pin down eyelids and bind arms and legs and stage the body in a box because if you just put a human cadaver anywhere, it flops like a rag doll.<br /> <br /> So when someone talks about using what is, for all intents and purposes, a corpse as a magical tool, all I can think is this really awkward hoisting of a body by what amounts to a highschool skeleton stand and using wires to pose the arms and legs in what is could qualify as the world's most heinous Thunderbirds homage but definitely not a magical ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your sensibilities. But then again, a Sarira is not really a corpse, often doesn't look like one, and there are compelling practical reasons to keep one intact, and anybody that dismembers one for petty gain is a shortsighted fool, same as with any other case of despoiling very valuable and non-renewable resources.<br /> <br /> By the way, this preview means there is progress for Signs of Sorcery at last, despite lying in seeming development limbo for almost a year. I am so excited and impatient about getting this book, since its content promises to be the 2nd volume of the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:11:40-08:00","id":1034811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034805#post1034805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for having 200 Mana, a normal Artifact contains mana equal to twice the dot rating. The write up says each Sarira dot possesses 10 points of mana. I believe 200 mana may also be an error and it should be 100. Either that or 20 points of mana per Sarira dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says it has 10 dots of Mana per dot of artifact, which would be 100. But it then says 'An intact Sarira accumulates 1 point per dot per century.' Which fits with how much Mana he has and him being alive around a thousand years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-19-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:14:58-08:00","id":1034814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034807#post1034807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand your sensibilities. But then again, a Sarira is not really a corpse, often doesn't look like one, and there are compelling practical reasons to keep one intact, and anybody that dismembers one for petty gain is a shortsighted fool, same as with any other case of despoiling very valuable and non-renewable resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but the description is sort of limited in that regard. The descriptions mention a granite statue as an example, and the King is very clearly a skeletal horror that'd make a good Sauron stand-in. I just can't get past the general idea of them being mistaken for a corpse, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034807#post1034807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, this preview means there is progress for Signs of Sorcery at last, despite lying in seeming development limbo for almost a year. I am so excited and impatient about getting this book, since its content promises to be the 2nd volume of the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:18:45-08:00","id":1034820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034811#post1034811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says it has 10 dots of Mana per dot of artifact, which would be 100. But it then says 'An intact Sarira accumulates 1 point per dot per century.' Which fits with how much Mana he has and him being alive around a thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1000 / 100 = 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:21:53-08:00","id":1034825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034811#post1034811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says it has 10 dots of Mana per dot of artifact, which would be 100. But it then says 'An intact Sarira accumulates 1 point per dot per century.' Which fits with how much Mana he has and him being alive around a thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's not how I first read accumulating mana. I wrote it off as naturally recovering mana over that time like a terrible hallow. That does fit - 10 mana per century, 10 centuries in 1,000 years, 100 extra mana. I still think that it's an oversight on the spells, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:22:38-08:00","id":1034827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034820#post1034820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1000 / 100 = 10</div> </div> </div> </div>Each dot has 10. 10 dots x 10 Mana = 100 Mana.<br /> <br /> Then it gains 1 Mana <i>per dot</i> every century. That's 10 Mana per century. 10 centuries, a thousand years, is a hundred Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:40:40-08:00","id":1034836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034814#post1034814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but the description is sort of limited in that regard. The descriptions mention a granite statue as an example, and the King is very clearly a skeletal horror that'd make a good Sauron stand-in. I just can't get past the general idea of them being mistaken for a corpse, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first visual cue would have been a golden Buddha statue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:48:09-08:00","id":1034847,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if you could make a golem out of it, and if so, then have that golem be controlled by a ghost or spirit or its own mind. And if so, would they be able to use the artifact's spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:59:25-08:00","id":1034854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034836#post1034836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first visual cue would have been a golden Buddha statue.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought at the mention of jewels is the remains of Saint Coronatus or Deodatus. Doesn't improve things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034847#post1034847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if you could make a golem out of it, and if so, then have that golem be controlled by a ghost or spirit or its own mind. And if so, would they be able to use the artifact's spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot. Very first thing said about them mechanically is that no spell can directly affect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:07:56-08:00","id":1034857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034854#post1034854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot. Very first thing said about them mechanically is that no spell can directly affect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural powers, too, so flat out Possession is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:10:56-08:00","id":1034860,"title":"","content":"It's more of a place holder for an Ascended Mate then a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:00:07-08:00","id":1034884,"title":"","content":"The guy who discovered the Throne is terrified of the Ascended being who left the Sarira behind. Which makes me wonder, if they are still connected is the Ascended able to &quot;cast&quot; through it? I mean they don't really need to because they can probably generate ochemata, but it'd be interesting if there were a a Samir's that keeps trying to cast Possession on passers by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:27:50-08:00","id":1035103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034807#post1034807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand your sensibilities. But then again, a Sarira is not really a corpse, often doesn't look like one, and there are compelling practical reasons to keep one intact, and anybody that dismembers one for petty gain is a shortsighted fool, same as with any other case of despoiling very valuable and non-renewable resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Sarira looks like this? If yes, I'm more than content with idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/indianajones/images/5/52/Crystal_skull_(13).jpg/revision/latest?cb=20100501164151\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Also - Crystal Skulls being confirmed to be ex-heads of Asended beings - yeah, let's collect our Atlanteans colleagues heads for their knowledge and memories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T00:24:07-08:00","id":1035114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1034884#post1034884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy who discovered the Throne is terrified of the Ascended being who left the Sarira behind. Which makes me wonder, if they are still connected is the Ascended able to &quot;cast&quot; through it? I mean they don't really need to because they can probably generate ochemata, but it'd be interesting if there were a a Samir's that keeps trying to cast Possession on passers by.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is always wise to assume that Exarchs and other Ascended mages have a few Ochemata at their beck and call to send in the Phenomenal World on some task. The trick is to understand which issues the Supernal being(s) in question would deem of sufficient importance to capture their attention and deliver an avatar to deal with, despite potential Pax concerns. It seems the King deems disrespect and misuse of their Sarira by warlords and petty sorcerer-kings a sufficiently important issue. The Throne might even be a source for those legends of seats or thrones killing anybody that sits on them but the chosen hero or king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-20-2017, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:33:12-08:00","id":1035769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1035114#post1035114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is always wise to assume that Exarchs and other Ascended mages have a few Ochemata at their beck and call to send in the Phenomenal World on some task. The trick is to understand which issues the Supernal being(s) in question would deem of sufficient importance to capture their attention and deliver an avatar to deal with, despite potential Pax concerns. It seems the King deems disrespect and misuse of their Sarira by warlords and petty sorcerer-kings a sufficiently important issue. The Throne might even be a source for those legends of seats or thrones killing anybody that sits on them but the chosen hero or king.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC The Pax doesn't actually apply to beings that have Ascended, only Archmasters and entities of similar power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:41:08-08:00","id":1035771,"title":"","content":"Do other beings have ochemata? I've only heard of them in relation to Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:00:36-08:00","id":1035775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1035771#post1035771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other beings have ochemata? I've only heard of them in relation to Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any archmaster, ascended or otherwise, with an Arcanum of 8+ can create an ochemata. However, ochemata of ascended beings like Exarchs are more powerful.<br /> <br /> The process is described in Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:04:40-08:00","id":1035778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1035771#post1035771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other beings have ochemata? I've only heard of them in relation to Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Ascended beings, as well as Archmages of sufficient power (i.e having the Imperial Practice of Dominions and eight dots in at least one Arcanum), can have and do use Ochemata. The issue is discussed at some length for Archmasters in Imperial Mysteries, and the book also says Ascended mages send Ochemata, e.g. it describes the Ochema of the Corpus Author.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:46:01-08:00","id":1037198,"title":"","content":"How much powerful Artfact will be Crystal Skulls if they will be parts of Sariras? How much would be Crystal Heart of once Ascended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:23:59-08:00","id":1037539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1037198#post1037198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much powerful Artfact will be Crystal Skulls if they will be parts of Sariras? How much would be Crystal Heart of once Ascended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what you want them to do, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:34:59-08:00","id":1037545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1037198#post1037198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much powerful Artfact will be Crystal Skulls if they will be parts of Sariras? How much would be Crystal Heart of once Ascended?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the ST, you assign the dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:08:44-08:00","id":1037612,"title":"","content":"I meant on what Artifacts Dots scale we talk about for chunks like Heart or Head of once Ascended? Divisible Ability seems to imply that any Size of organ you are chopping does not mean anything on Artifact Dot level - that is not very helpful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Divisible:</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Despite their resistance to supernatural powers, Sariras can be chopped into pieces and even destroyed with steady hands and sharp tools. An intact Sarira possesses Structure 50, Durability 5. Each dot of Artifact power maintains the same Durability, and 5 Structure; a 3-dot portion possess Structure 15, for instance. A piece's power and relative toughness isn't related to its Size, but its symbolic importance. A leg might be less potent than a petrified pineal gland.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Every 5 points of damage reduces a Sarira's Artifact powers by 1 dot, and releases its Mana portion per dot (see below) back to the Supernal Realms.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Separating a Sarira into pieces in any methodical fashion requires a successful Dexterity + Occult roll, with a risk of Dramatic Failure, for a process that requires one hour of careful work. Dramatic Failure inflicts 5 points of damage, with the aforementioned consequences. Successes scored indicate the maximum Artifact dots that can be separated, with an absolute limit of 5, though the mage can opt to cut away something with a lower rating of her choice. Having at it with an ax, a prayer and no dice roll, automatically inflicts 5 points of damage and the attendant consequences over the course of an hour, and separates a piece as powerful as the Storyteller wants it to be. (By default, roll a die and halve the result, rounding up. The piece has that many dots.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chopping up a Sarira is a Low Act of Hubris. The mage mars a physical sign of Ascension and risks destroying it.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>But let's assume that Size of organ does have meaning to chopped Artifact - What power do we see in Head or Heart? Heart is surely Size 1 thing, but should not Head be Size 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:49:01-08:00","id":1037638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034596-preview-sariras-relics-of-ascension?p=1037612#post1037612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant on what Artifacts Dots scale we talk about for chunks like Heart or Head of once Ascended? Divisible Ability seems to imply that any Size of organ you are chopping does not mean anything on Artifact Dot level - that is not very helpful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But let's assume that Size of organ does have meaning to chopped Artifact - What power do we see in Head or Heart? Heart is surely Size 1 thing, but should not Head be Size 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems Size indeed has nothing to do with a Sarira's ability or its potency. When chopping off the corpse-shaped Sarira's head, you decide how much dots it takes from the total, limited by the method you choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T23:13:01-08:00","id":1037686,"title":"","content":"Line: <i>'Successes scored indicate the maximum Artifact dots that can be separated, with an absolute limit of 5, though the mage can opt to cut away something with a lower rating of her choice.' </i>- Seems to indicate that maximum Artifacts dots of each part can be 5. With rules of Artifact Merit, it seems to indicate one spell of 5th dot, or multiple combinations with lower spells.<br /> <br /> So those Head or Heart can have one Master spell or few lower spells. I wonder what would it be to store Rotes in it - would it simply work as Sarira part having spell itself to cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}